  data: {
    LLM: "Starting Hand Selection: Only play if your first three cards are both 8 or lower with no pair. If your hole card is paired with your upcard, or if you show a high card like a King or Queen, strongly consider folding.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Low: If your two hole cards are an A and a 2, and your up-card is a Jack, your hand looks weak to opponents. Use this to induce bluffs from players with 'cleaner' 3rd-street up-cards.\n\nPot-Limit Pressure: Since it's Pot-Limit, if you have a lock on the low (e.g., you show 3-4-5-6 and hold an Ace), bet the maximum to force opponents who have 5-6-7-8 to either pay a premium or fold their second-best draws.",
    Player: "Starting Hand Selection: Only play if your first three cards are both 8 or lower with no pair. If your hole card is paired with your upcard, or if you show a high card like a King or Queen, strongly consider folding.\n\nThe 'Hidden' Low: If your two hole cards are an A and a 2, and your up-card is a Jack, your hand looks weak to opponents. Use this to induce bluffs from players with 'cleaner' 3rd-street up-cards.\n\nPot-Limit Pressure: Since it's Pot-Limit, if you have a lock on the low (e.g., you show 3-4-5-6 and hold an Ace), bet the maximum to force opponents who have 5-6-7-8 to either pay a premium or fold their second-best draws.",
