    advanced: "Pot-Limit Pressure: Since it's Pot-Limit, if you have a lock on the low (e.g., you show 3-4-5-6 and hold an Ace), bet the maximum to force opponents who have 5-6-7-8 to either pay a premium or fold their second-best draws.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In Lowball, the Ace is your most valuable card. If you see three Aces showing among your opponents' up-cards, your own Ace-high draw becomes much stronger (as they are less likely to have an Ace in the hole).",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Don't chase a 9-low if the pot is large and your opponent is showing the potential for a 7-low. You are 'drawing dead' in many scenarios.",
      },
    ],
  },
